, "confidence": "medium", "notes": []}, "overview": "Texas's 9th District is a new seat created by the state's partisan redistricting, and no incumbent holds it. Republican Alex Mealer, a Trump-backed candidate who won a contested primary runoff, faces Democrat Leticia Gutierrez. The district carries a nine-point Republican lean, and the political environment this year also favors the GOP.\n\nMealer has raised more than $2 million and benefits from nearly $5 million in outside support, while Gutierrez has raised under $60,000 with no outside spending. Two polls show Mealer ahead by six points, and prediction markets give her roughly an 84% chance. Every major race rater labels the seat Likely R or stronger for Republicans, making Gutierrez's path to an upset narrow.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -8.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0891, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0766, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1178, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0737, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0642, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0775, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0899, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0901, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0919, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1301, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1157, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1517, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0727, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0914, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0573, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0729, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.068, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0897, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0922, "margin": -9.0}, {"date":